# Structured question popups (dual-host)

Call a structured question tool — never paste option lists as plain
chat when any of these exist in the tool schema:

| Priority | Tool | Host / source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | **AskQuestion** | Cursor host tool (ACP `cursor/ask_question`) |
| 2 | **AskUserQuestion** | Claude Code host |
| 3 | **ask_user_question** | MCP `vgv-ask-question` (form elicitation) |
| 4 | Numbered chat list | Last resort only |

Detect by **tool availability**, not by guessing the product name.

## Critical: AskQuestion is host-injected + model-gated

Cursor attaches **AskQuestion** to the agent tool schema. Plugins, rules,
and MCP **cannot** add it. Staff-confirmed availability:

| Model / routing | AskQuestion |
| --- | --- |
| **Composer 2.5** | Yes |
| Claude / GPT | Usually yes |
| **Grok 4.5** | **No** (all modes, intentional) |
| **Auto** (may route to Grok) | Unreliable |

MCP `ask_user_question` is a **different** UI path (MCP elicitation). It
does **not** turn on AskQuestion. If elicitation fails, it returns
numbered text.

For brainstorm / plan / refine handoffs that need the **native clickable
card**, pin the chat model to **Composer 2.5** (not Auto, not Grok).

## Skills format is NOT chat output

VGV skills often show markdown Options blocks. Those are tool input —
map each option to `{ id, label }` and call the highest-priority tool.

## Required behavior

1. Call **AskQuestion** if it is in the tool schema.
2. Else call **AskUserQuestion** if available.
3. Else call MCP **`ask_user_question`** with
   `{ questions: [{ id, prompt, options }] }`.
4. Mark the recommended option clearly (e.g. "(Recommended)").
5. Do **not** paste options as plain chat when any tool above exists.
6. On Cursor, never offer clear-context options — use `Plan now`,
   `Build now`, `Continue in this chat`, or `Stop here` only.
7. After a Cursor handoff selection, invoke the next skill in this chat.
8. If **none** of the tools exist, use a short numbered list.

## When AskQuestion is missing on Cursor

You may tell the user once, briefly: pin **Composer 2.5** for the native
picker (Grok / Auto often omit AskQuestion). Then still call MCP
`ask_user_question` if present.

Do **not** claim MCP “covers” or “replaces” AskQuestion.

## Handoff options

Post-brainstorm / post-plan / post-build option lists come from the
active skill. Present them via the host tool when available, else MCP,
then execute the pick per `vgv-cursor-handoff.mdc`.
